{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You shall not murder.</b> These five utterances, which are five negative prohibitions, were on the second tablet. And now I shall explain to you their arrangement and their interpretation and how they are linked one to another. After He warned above concerning idolatry by way of prohibition, He mentioned here: לא תרצח לא תנאף — for so is their arrangement according to their punishment, and so do the Rabbis, of blessed memory, always mention them: idolatry, and bloodshed, and illicit sexual relations. And when it says לא תגנוב, the verse speaks of kidnapping — a matter that carries liability to court-imposed death — like murder and adultery. And after murder and adultery He warned concerning theft and false testimony and coveting, which is included in חמדה. And the order of these prohibitions is that each preceding one is more severe, and therefore they were arranged in this correct sequence." "<b>You shall not answer against your fellow.</b> It did not say 'against your brother' (אחיך), as is the practice of the verses (Deuteronomy 23:20): לא תשיך לאחיך, (ibid. 23:22): לכל אבדת אחיך, and similar cases — for there we interpret 'your brother' and not an idolater, whereas here He warned even concerning the idolater, for so we find (Exodus 11:2): וישאלו איש מאת רעהו — and that was said concerning the Egyptians. Moreover, had it said 'your brother' (אחיך), it would appear that testimony is valid from relatives, for He would be warning us only against false testimony, whereas true testimony would be valid — but the matter is not so, for all testimony from relatives is disqualified, whether it be false or true, whether for one's benefit or for one's loss. And the verse should have said: לא תענה ברעך עדות שקר — 'you shall not answer against your fellow false testimony'; had it said so, the warning would apply only to the witness himself, that he himself not testify falsely. But since it said עד שקר, it is thereby explained that this is a warning not to scheme to bring a false witness, and this is the sense of לא תענה — do not assist and do not bring against your fellow a false witness to testify against him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:40.656177843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}